# armour/woman/brigandine: the brigandine on the woman (ARMOUR-W wave 2 r1 from ARMOUR-M's man, cut to HER plate; STYLE_P2 25.2, 28.4, 29.6; PLAN 'The envelope in
# production'). A dyed cloth coat with steel plates riveted inside: the coat in the accent slot (the people's colour, as
# rig 1's kingdom-coloured brigandine), the plate courses shown by a seam and a row of rivet heads (metal 2, lit side step
# 3, shadow side step 2), a steel gorget at the neck, the belt; the sleeves are the tunic's (regionsOf: cloth1). Until
# wave 2 brigandine fell back to plate's steel cuirass (doll_resolve's chain): a River or Highland soldier read as plate.
# The base views keep plate's mask in every key (no outline or fit change); every `when` view (the T5 / T6 / Mythic
# surcoats and cuirasses) is plate's own, copied, so a masterwork reads as it did; plate's `cut-*` chest overlays are NOT
# carried (they paint a steel breastplate over the coat: the cloth would read as plate again).
# Finish regions as plate's (R the gorget's rim and the hem, P the lit chest, G the socket, N the lower edge, W the wear).
# Generated by ARMOUR-W tools/gen_brig_w.py (ARMOUR-M's generator on her maps) from plate.pxm; re-run, never hand-edit. Format: rpg/art/doll/doll.h.
use person
body woman
role armour brigandine
layer torso
anchor neck
keys torso
z 2
legend Q linen 0
legend R linen 1
legend S linen 2
legend T linen 3
legend U linen 4
legend J cloak 0
legend D cloak 1
legend H cloak 2
legend I cloak 3
legend X cloak 4
legend k device 1
legend l device 2
legend F device 3
legend ! glow 2
legend % glow 3


